Page 230 abrigar: Found match for regex: =
Page 230 abrigar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Most likely from {{inh|ca|LL.|aprīcō|aprīcāre}} (compare the form {{m|pro|abriar}} and {{cog|oc|abrigar}}), from {{inh|ca|la|aprīcor|aprīcārī}}<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref>, from {{m|la|aprīcus}}. Compare {{cog|es|abrigar}}, {{cog|en|apricate}}, and {{cog|fr|abrier}}.

Alternatively, and less likely, from {{inh|ca|LL.|*abrigāre||to cover, shelter}}, from {{m|la|a-}} + {{m|la|brigare|}}, from {{der|ca|frk|*biwrīhan|*birīhan|t=to cover, protect}}, from {{der|ca|gem-pro|*bi-}} + {{m|gem-pro|*wrīhaną||to cover, clothe}}, from {{der|ca|ine-pro|*werk'-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*werg'-||to twist, weave, tie together}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|birīhan||to cover}}, {{cog|ang|bewrēon||to cover, enwrap, protect}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-abrigar.wav|Audio (Catalonia)}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}

# to [[wrap up]], to [[cover]]
# to [[keep]] [[warm]]
# to [[shelter]]

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj-ar|abrig}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|abric}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
* {{R:ca:DNV}}
* {{R:ca:DCVB}}

-------- end text --------
