|t=Adding their demands to hundreds of thousands of people expressing their rage for the death of the '''African-American''' George Floyd in Minneapolis and other cities in the United States, many posters read "BLM" ("Black lives matter") or "I can't breathe"; words which both George Floyd and Adama Traoré spoke before dying.
