===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
[[File:Arna de canya.jpg|thumb|{{sense|beehive}} arna]]
Probably from {{der|ca|cel-pro|*arona}} (“ring” or “wheel”) due to these structures first being built in a cylindrical form from woven wood or vegetation.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[beehive]]
#: {{syn|ca|buc|casera|rusc}}
# {{synonym of|ca|arnot}}

=====Holonyms=====
* {{sense|beehive}} {{l|ca|apiari}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|arnot}}

===Etymology 2===
{{unk|ca}} origin, but possibly cognate to {{cog|eu|arr||worm, insect}}. Cognate to {{cog|oc|arna}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[moth]]

=====See also=====
* {{l|ca|eruga|gloss=caterpillar}}
* {{l|ca|papallona|gloss=butterfly}}

===Etymology 3===
Possibly the same origin as Etymology 2 above, but also possibly by refactoring of {{m|ca|sarna||scabies}} as {{m|ca|s'|s’}} + ''arna''.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f}}

# {{lb|ca|Mallorca}} [[dandruff]]
#: {{syn|ca|caspa}}

