===Etymology===
{{bor+|ca|rmq|calé}}, plural of {{m|rmq|caló}}, from {{der|ca|rom|kalo}}, from {{der|ca|sa|काल|t=dark, black}}. The term originally referred to "dark" copper coins in contrast to "light" silver coins, which were called {{m|rmq|parné}}, from {{m|rmq|parnó||white}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m|#s}}

# {{lb|ca|colloquial|usually|in the plural}} [[money]], [[cash]]
#: {{syn|ca|diner}}
#* {{quote-journal|ca|journal=Time Out Barcelona|date=Feb 27 2020|volume=586|title=Compartir és estimar|author=Erica Aspas|page=22
|passage=Abans de comprar l'estri que teniu a les mans, penseu: realment em fa falta? Us deixareu els '''calés''' en una cosa que potser només feu servir un dia o uns minuts?
|t=Before buying the tool that you have in your hands, think: do I really need it? Will you let your '''money''' go something that you might only use for one day or a few minutes?
|url=https://digitalarchive.timeout.com/Europe/Spain/Barcelona/2020/February/TOB_586/DVL/reader.html}}

