Page 4741 canet: Found match for regex: =
Page 4741 canet: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{af|ca|ca|-et}}. In the sense of "five-cent coin", from the resemblance of the device of a lion to a dog. (Compare Castilian {{m|es|perra chica}}.) The card game takes its name from the coin.
[[File:España Gobierno Provisional 1870 5 Centimos.jpg|thumb|''canet'' (moneda de 5 cèntims)]]

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{diminutive of|ca|ca||dog}}
# {{lb|ca|obsolete}} a five-cent coin
# a card game

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|ca|fr|canette}}, with a change of gender.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# a [[mug]] for beer with a capacity of one liter
# a round earthenware [[jug]] for liquor, especially gin

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:GDLC}}

{{C|ca|Card games|Coins|Vessels}}

