===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|caure}}, from {{inh|ca|la|cadō|cadere}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*kadō}}, from {{der|ca|ine-pro|*ḱh₂d-||to fall}}. Old Catalan also had a variant {{m|roa-oca|caér}}, from a Late Latin variant {{m|la|cadeo|cadēre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-caure.wav|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|ca|awɾe|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|pres_1_sg=caic|past_part=caigut}}

# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall]] {{gloss|to come down, to drop, to descend}}
#* {{quote-web
|ca
|date=2019-10-12
|author=
|title=Rècord històric en una marató: Kipchoge destrossa el mur de les dues hores
|work=Diari de Girona
|url=https://www.diaridegirona.cat/esports/2019/10/12/record-historic-marato-kipchoge-destrossa/1007679.html
|passage=El kenyà Eliud Kipchoge, rècord mundial de marató, va fer '''caure''' aquest dissabte a Viena el llegendari mur de les dues hores sobre la distància amb un temps de 1h59: 40, una marca que no obstant això no serà oficial per les ajudes externes que va rebre.}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall]] {{gloss|to move to a lower position due to gravity}}
# to [[fall]] (upon) {{gloss|to arrive through chance, fate, or inheritance}}
# {{lb|ca|with {{l|ca|a}}}} to [[fall into]] {{gloss|to go into something by falling}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall into]] {{gloss|to enter a negative state}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall into]], to [[fall for]]; to be [[ensnare]]d by
#: {{ux|ca|'''caure''' en temptació|'''to fall''' into temptation}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall down]], to [[collapse]] {{gloss|to fall to the ground}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall]] {{gloss|to become}}
#: {{ux|ca|'''caure''' malalt|'''to fall''' ill}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall]], to [[collapse]] {{gloss|to be overthrown or defeated}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to be [[grant]]ed or [[award]]ed
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[fall on]] {{gloss|to occur on a particular day}}

