Page 6078 collar: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|ca|LL.|collāre||an unattached item worn about the neck}}, from {{der|ca|la|collāris}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|a chain or belt placed around the neck of an animal}}
# a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|a solid circle of metal placed around the neck of a slave or prisoner}}
# a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|any ornament placed at the neck}}
# {{lb|ca|historical}} a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|a gold chain worn about the neck as a badge of belonging to certain chivalric orders}}
# a [[necklace]]
#: {{syn|ca|collaret}}
# {{lb|ca|historical|military}} an [[aventail]]
# a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|a ring or loop used to support and protect a rotating shaft}}
# a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|a ring or loop used to join together two parts of a shaft or pole}}
# {{lb|ca|entomology}} a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|lobed membranous expansion of the prothorax of some insects}}
# {{lb|ca|zoology}} a {{l|en|collar}} {{gloss|a band of feathers, fur, or scales about the neck of an animal that is of a contrasting color to what is near it}}

===Etymology 2===
From the action of securing a [[yoke]] around the {{m|ca|coll||neck}} of an animal.

====Verb====
{{ca-verb}}

# to join together objects through the use of nuts or bolts
# to {{l|en|collar}} a person or animal
# to establish control of a person or animal
# to [[twist]] {{gloss|to pressure someone}}
# to [[screw]] {{gloss|to tighten a screw}}
# {{lb|ca|textiles}} to adjust a {{m|ca|collador||heddle}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ca-conj-ar|coll}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|to collar an animal}} {{l|ca|enjovar}}, {{l|ca|junyir}}
* {{sense|to establish control}} {{l|ca|sotmetre}}, {{l|ca|subjectar}}

