===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|colde}}, from pre-literary {{m|roa-oca||*coude}} (with hypercorrection of coda [w] to [ɫ]), from {{inh|ca|la|cubitum}}. Compare the development of Catalan {{m|ca|malalt}}, {{m|ca|delme}} from original {{m|roa-oca|malaute}}, {{m|roa-oca|deume}} (Latin {{m|la|male habitus}}, {{m|la|decimus}}). The subsequent change from /d/ to /(d)z/ may have been by analogy with {{m|ca|polze||thumb}}. {{doublet|ca|cúbit}}, a borrowing from Latin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ca|/ˈkɔlzə/|[ˈkɔɫzə]|qual=Barcelona, Berga}}
* {{IPA|ca|/ˈkolze/|[ˈkoɫze]|qual=Andorra, Girona, La Seu d'Urgell, Alicante}}
* {{IPA|ca|/ˈkolse/|[ˈkoɫse]|qual=Valencia}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-colze.wav|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[elbow]]
# [[cubit]], {{ngd|an informal unit of length based on the distance of a forearm and hand}}
# {{lb|ca|historical}} [[codo]], [[Spanish]] [[cubit]], {{ngd|a traditional unit of length equivalent to about 41.6 cm}}
# {{lb|ca|golf}} [[dogleg]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|colzada}}
* {{l|ca|recolzar}}

