===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|at}}

===Etymology 1===
From the participle of the obsolete Catalan verb {{m|ca|croar||to cross}}.

====Adjective====
{{ca-adj}}

# {{lb|ca|obsolete}} having the shape of a [[cross]]
# {{lb|ca|obsolete}} decorated with one or more [[cross]]es

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ca|creuat}}

====Noun====
[[File:Pedro III croat 612529.jpg|thumb|a croat of [[w:Peter III of Aragon|Pere II de Barcelona]] minted in 1285]]
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{lb|ca|historical|military}} [[crusader]] {{gloss|a Christian warrior who went on a crusade}}
# {{lb|ca|obsolete|_|but later revived}} [[crusader]] {{gloss|anyone engaged in a concerted effort to do good}}
# {{lb|ca|historical|numismatics}} a [[silver]] coin of the [[w:County of Barcelona|County of Barcelona]] minted from 1285 to 1706 and worth 12 [[diner#Catalan|diners]], so named on account of the large cross on the [[reverse]]

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ca|croada|gloss=crusade}}

====See also====
* {{pedia|lang=ca|Croat (moneda)}}

