Page 8611 dir: Found match for regex: =
Page 8611 dir: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|dire||Northern Catalan|Algherese}}
* {{alt|ca|diure||Algherese}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|la|dīcō|dīcere}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*deikō}}, from {{inh|ca|ine-pro|*déyḱti||to show, point out}}. Compare {{cog|oc|dire}} or {{m|oc|díser}}, {{cog|fr|dire}}, and {{cog|es|decir}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-dir.wav|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|pres_1_sg=dic}}

# {{lb|ca|transitive|intransitive}} to [[say]], to [[pronounce]]
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[say]], to [[tell]]
#: {{ux|ca|Va '''dir''' una mentida.|She '''told''' a lie.}}
#: {{ux|ca|El '''dèiem''' que cuinés el sopar.|We '''told''' him to cook dinner.}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[call]], to [[refer]] to as
# {{lb|ca|reflexive}} to be [[name]]d, to be [[call]]ed
#: {{uxi|ca|Com et '''dius'''?|What's your name?}}

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj-ure-ia2|d|i<!--
-->|infinitive=dir<!--
-->|past_part=dit<!--

-->|impr_2_sg=digues<!--
-->|impr_2_pl=digueu<!--
-->}}

Balearic has {{m|ca|deis}} as the second-person plural present indicative form. This is similar to {{cog|fr|dire}} having {{m|fr|dites}} as the standard form instead of the expected {{m|fr|disez}}, and contemporary {{cog|it|dire}} having {{m|it|dite}} as the standard form in place of the expected {{m|it|dicete}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|dir-se}}
* {{l|ca|és a dir}}
* {{l|ca|voler dir}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|dicció}}
* {{l|ca|dictar}}
* {{l|ca|entredir}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
* {{R:ca:GDLC}}
* {{R:ca:DNV}}
* {{R:ca:DCVB}}

-------- end text --------
