Page 10457 escot: Found match for regex: =
Page 10457 escot: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|ca|fro|escot}}, from {{der|ca|frk|*skot||monetary contribution}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|ò}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[share]] {{gloss|the portion held by one person of a financial commitment that was made jointly with others}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|escotar|gloss=to pay one's share}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|ca|acció|gloss=a share of stock}}
* {{l|ca|quota|gloss=membership fee}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|ca|escotar||to make or wear clothing with décolletage that exposes cleavage}}. Note that despite the similarities in pronunciation, and that they both deal with clothing around the neck, the English word {{m|en|ascot}} has no etymological connection to the Catalan word {{m|ca||escot}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|ó}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[décolletage]] {{gloss|a low neckline that exposes cleavage}}
#: {{syn|ca|escotat}}
# [[cleavage]] {{gloss|the portion of the bust and back that is left uncovered because it is above the neckline of a dress}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{der|ca|la|Scotus|Scot-}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m|f=+}}

# {{lb|ca|historical}} {{w|Scoti|Scotus}}; a member of the Goidelic peoples that raided Roman Britain from Ireland, and then in the Early Middle Ages invaded and settled Western Scotland
# {{lb|ca|archaic}} [[Scot]] {{gloss|a native of Scotland}}
#: {{syn|ca|escocès}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ca|Escòcia}}

===Usage notes===
The etymologies of the noun {{m|ca||escot}} and the verb {{m|ca|escotar}} are intertwined. In Etymology 1, the noun is the root form and the verb is derived from it, while in Etymology 2, the verb is the root form and the noun is derived from it.

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
* {{R:ca:GDLC}}
* {{R:ca:DNV}}
* {{R:ca:DCVB}}

{{C|ca|Anatomy|Clothing|Demonyms|Economics|Nationalities}}
-------- end text --------
