Page 14219 hom: Found match for regex: =
Page 14219 hom: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|hom}}, from the nominative case of {{inh|ca|la|homō||man}}. Its pronominal use is of {{cog|gem}} origin. Compare {{cog|ang|man||one, they, people}}, reduced form of {{cog|ang|mann||man, person}}; {{cog|fr|on}}; {{cog|de|man||one, they, people}}; {{cog|nl|men||one, they, people}}.

Doublet of {{m|ca|home||man}}, from {{inh|ca|roa-oca|(h)ome(n)}}, that continues the accusative case form {{m|la|hominem|}}. There are very few Latin nouns that have been inherited in more than one case form, others include {{m|ca|drac|}}/{{m|ca|dragó|}} and {{m|ca|res|}}/{{m|ca|re|}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|ò}}

===Pronoun===
{{ca-ppron}}

# [[one]], [[people]], [[someone]] {{gloss|an unspecified individual: indefinite personal pronoun}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Hom''' diu que…|It is said that…}}

====Declension====
{{ca-decl-ppron}}

====See also====
* {{l|ca|tu}}
* {{l|ca|u}}

{{cln|ca|terms inherited from Latin nominatives}}

