{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{lb|ca|linguistics}} a feature found in varieties of Eastern Catalan whereby the Vulgar Latin medial clusters ''c'l'', ''g'l'', ''t'l'', and ''ly'' (from ''le'' and ''li'' before vowels) yield the consonant [j] instead of the [ʎ] found in other varieties. For instance, {{m|ca|llentia}} instead of {{m|ca|llentilla}}
#: {{syn|ca|ieisme històric|iodització}}
# {{lb|ca|linguistics}} More generally, pronunciation of etymological [ʎ] as [j], as in Modern French and most contemporary varieties of Spanish

