The letter {{m|mul|k}} is not normally used in Catalan. Instead, Catalan orthography calls for using the {{m|mul|qu}} digraph to represent the {{IPAchar|/k/}} sound before an {{m|mul|e}} or an {{m|mul|i}}. Therefor, when the metric system was introduced into Catalan, the prefix {{m|fr|kilo-}} was originally spelled {{m|ca|quilo-}}. With the advent of {{m|en|k}} as a standard international abbreviation, usage of {{m|en||kilo-}} has become not only acceptable, but also more common than the traditional spelling. However, traditionalists still insist upon the use of {{m|ca|quilo-}}.

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
* {{R:ca:GDLC}}
* {{R:ca:DNV}}

{{C|ca|SI units}}

-------- end text --------
