{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|palissa}} 'fence, palisade' (especially in the context of jousting), either borrowed from {{der|ca|es|paliza}}<ref>{{R:ca:DCVB}}</ref> or an indigenous formation,<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref> in either case etymologically {{der|ca|la|pālus||stake}} and perhaps {{m|la||-icea}}. The change from /l/ to /ʎ/ is likely by analogy with {{m|ca|lliça}} or {{m|ca|vall}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[beating]]

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ca|palissada}}
* {{l|ca|pal}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{af|ca|palla|-issa}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[hayloft]]
#: {{syn|ca|herbera|paller}}

