Page 20327 Pasqua: Found match for regex: =
Page 20327 Pasqua: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|VL.||pascua}}, from {{inh|ca|LL.|pascha}} (influenced by {{m|la|pascua}} 'pastures, grazing', perhaps because of the bitter herbs of the Passover seder or the end of fasting for Lent at Easter), from {{der|ca|grc|πάσχα}}, ultimately from {{der|ca|he|פסח||Passover|sc=Hebr|tr=pésakh}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Millars-Pasqua.wav|Audio (Valencian)}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[Easter]]
#: {{syn|ca|Pasqua de Resurrecció|Pasqua Florida|primera Pasqua}}
# [[Pentecost]]
#: {{syn|ca|Pasqua de Pentecosta|Pasqua Granada|Pentecosta|segona Pasqua}}

====Usage notes====
When used without qualifier this word usually means Easter and not Pentecost. When uncapitalized, ''[[pasqua#Catalan|pasqua]]'' refers to [[Passover]].

