Page 20677 per: Found match for regex: =
Page 20677 per: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|per}}, from {{inh|ca|la|per}}, appropriating the senses of Latin {{m|la|prō}} as well.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Balearic|Central}} {{IPA|ca|/pəɾ/}}
* {{a|Valencian}} {{IPA|ca|/peɾ/}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-per.wav|Audio}}

===Preposition===
{{head|ca|preposition}}

# [[through]], [[via]]: {{non-gloss definition|used in indicating the medium through which passage occurs}}
# [[at]], [[during]], [[in]]: {{non-gloss definition|used in indicating the time at which an event occurs}}
# [[during]], [[for]]: {{non-gloss definition|used in indicating the duration of time for which an event occurs}}
# [[because]], [[because of]]: {{non-gloss definition|used in indicating the reason an action was undertaken}}
# {{lb|ca|when followed by a verbal noun}} {{non-gloss definition|used in indicating the activity one intends to do because of an action}}
#: {{ux|ca|El meu germà anirà a Tahití '''per''' vacar a la platja.|My brother will go to Tahiti ('''in order''') to vacation on the beach.}}
# [[by]]: {{non-gloss definition|used in indicating the agent responsible for an action}}
# for [[each]]; for [[every]]
# [[a]], [[for]], {{l|en|per}}: {{non-gloss definition|used in indicating a rate of exchange}}

====Usage notes====
* When the preposition {{m|ca||per}} is followed by a masculine definite article, {{m|ca|el|g=s}}  or {{m|ca|els|g=p}}, it is contracted with it to the forms {{m|ca|pel|g=s}} or {{m|ca|pels|g=p}} respectively. If {{m|ca|el}} would be elided to the form {{m|ca|l'|l’}} because it is before a word beginning with a vowel, the elision to {{m|ca||per l’}} takes precedence over contracting to {{m|ca|pel}}.

====Derived terms====
