===Etymology===
From {{af|ca|picapedra|-ell}}. So named from the cry of "Picapedrell, qui té l'anell?" ("Grey heron, who has the ring?"), which is the signal to begin the guessing phase of the game.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m}}

# a children's game in which a ring is secretly passed from hand to hand until a signal is given to begin guessing and then one player has to guess which of the other players has it

