===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|VL.|pottum}}, {{m|la|pottus||pot, jar}}, from {{der|ca|frk|*pott}}, from {{der|ca|gem-pro|*puttaz||pot}}, from {{der|ca|ine-pro|*budnós||a type of vessel}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fr|pot}}, {{cog|en|pot}}, {{cog|stq|Pot}}, {{cog|nl|pot}}, {{cog|nds-de|Pott}}, {{cog|de|Pott}}, {{cog|sv|potta||chamber pot}}, {{cog|is|pottur||tub, pot}}, {{cog|xcl|պոյտն||pot, earthen pot}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[jar]], [[canister]], [[vessel]]
# [[jackpot]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|potet||little jar}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ca|VL.|*pote|*pote(t)}}, regularized form of {{der|ca|CL.|*potest}}. The reglularized pattern is present in all the Romance languages, see {{m|VL.|possō}}.

