===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-quart.wav|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|ca|aɾt|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{ca-adj}}

# {{lb|ca|ordinal}} [[fourth]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|fraction}} {{l|ca|quarter}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|quart creixent}} {{sense|waxing quarter moon}}
* {{l|ca|quart minvant}} {{sense|waning quarter moon}}
* {{l|ca|quart de rodó}} {{sense|quarter round molding}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{lb|ca|fractional}} [[quarter]] hour
# a political subdivision of the parishes [[:w:La Massana|La Massana]], [[:w:Ordino|Ordino]]{{,}} and [[:w:Sant Julià de Lòria|Sant Julià de Lòria]] in [[Andorra]]
# {{lb|ca|obsolete}} [[barrel]]; unit of liquid measure equal to one-quarter of a [[pipe]]
# {{lb|ca|paper}} [[quarto]]; paper size
# {{lb|ca|printing}} [[quarto]]; book size
# {{lb|ca|castells}} a [[casteller]] on the fourth level of a [[castell]]

====Usage notes====
Particularly in Catalonia, it is common to tell time by counting quarters of the '''next''' hour. For example:
: 2:15 ''un quart de tres'' (= ''dos i quart'')
: 2:30 ''dos quarts de tres'' (= ''dos i mitja'')
: 2:45 ''tres quarts de tres'' (= ''tres menys quart'' = ''falta un quart per a les tres'')
The equivalents given in parentheses are more common in Valencia and the Balearic Islands.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|quartà}}
* {{l|ca|quartal}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|quartilla}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}

{{C|ca|Geography|Time|Units of measure}}

