Page 26623 ton: Found match for regex: =
Page 26623 ton: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|ton}}, from {{inh|ca|VL.||*tum}}, reduced form of {{inh|ca|la|tuus|tuum}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*towos}}. Compare {{cog|oc,fr|ton}}.

In unstressed position in Vulgar Latin {{m|la||tuum, tuam}} etc. were monosyllabic and regularly became {{m|ca||ton, ta}} etc. in Catalan. When stressed they were disyllabic and became {{m|ca|teu}}, {{m|roa-oca|tua}} > {{m|ca|teua}} etc.

===Determiner===
{{head|ca|determiner|cat2=possessive determiners|g=m|feminine|ta|masculine plural|tos|feminine plural|tes}}

# [[your]] (singular)

====Usage notes====
{{ca-poss-determiner-note}}

The standard masculine plural form is ''tos'', but {{m|ca|tons}} can be found in some dialects.

===See also===
* {{l|ca|teu}}

===References===
* {{R:ca:DCVB}}

-------- end text --------
