===Etymology===
From {{inh-lite|ca|la|unum|ūnum|one}}, accusative form of {{m-lite|la|unus|ūnus|one}}, from {{inh-lite|ca|itc-ola|oinos}}, from {{inh-lite|ca|itc-pro|sc=Latinx|*oinos}}, from {{inh-lite|ca|ine-pro|sc=Latinx|*óynos}}. Romance cognates include {{cog-lite|oc|un}}. Also related to {{cog-lite|en|one}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-un.wav|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|ca|un|s=1}}

===Article===
{{head-lite|ca|articles|g=m|feminine|una|masculine plural|uns|feminine plural|unes}}

# [[an]]; the [[indefinite article]]
# {{lb|ca|in the plural}} [[some]]

====Usage notes====
* Unlike English, Catalan uses the indefinite article with plural nouns as well as singular nouns.
{{U:ca:cardinal numbers}}

===Numeral===
{{ca-num|una|u}}

# {{lb|ca|cardinal}} [[one]]

===Pronoun===
{{head-lite|ca|pronouns|g=m-s|feminine|una}}

# [[one]]; [[indefinite pronoun]]

====Derived terms====
