Page 28196 viuda: Found match for regex: =
Page 28196 viuda: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{dercat|ca|itc-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
Ultimately from {{der|ca|la|vidua}}. In the Middle Ages, jurists introduced a learned Latin borrowing {{m|roa-oca|vídua}} to replace the inherited Old Catalan form {{m|roa-oca|viuva}} (from a Vulgar Latin {{m|la|*viduva}}). The current form {{m|ca||viuda}} supposedly emerged as a compromise between the two forms<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC|viudo}}</ref>. The masculine form was derived from the feminine. Cf. also {{cog|es|viuda}}, which may have influenced it.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Adjective===
{{head|ca|adjective form|g=f-s}}

# {{inflection of|ca|viudo||f|s}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|f|m=viudo}}

# [[widow]]
# [[eagle ray]]
#: {{syn|ca|milana}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|vidu}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
